- Concurrency without parallelism: multiple threads execute in turn on a single\-core CPU;
- Concurrency with parallelism: multiple threads compute simultaneously on a multi\-core CPU;
- Use parallel algorithms, but do not manually create threads: let the standard library or the underlying runtime decide how to execute\.
